+// Bit 2 HOLD (alone, not with bit 1; Shared Mem layout): slim layout only, a P.n-bit team-word field (spare_alloc after camp news);
+// bit s = 1 while body s is alive, shows a fight/retreat/coming code and still targets the group it last published. Readers keep
+// slot s's last group while its code is >= 100 and its bit is 1. Field not allocated: that game plays bit 1's rule.
+// Bit 4 ERRAND HOLD (spec amendments 23:44Z + Shared Mem final rule): the HOLD bit is also 1 from the turn body s's digit goes from
+// a group to 0 on a recall channel, low-HP retreat, heal hold or shop recall turn, while those turns last, at most 10 rounds; the
+// field fits on either layout (no reader fallback without it). Readers keep
